This package embeds the OxiDB database engine ("the Engine") in your
application's process. The Engine is source-available software (see the
LICENSE in the OxiDB repository); its terms make one thing commercial,
and an embedded package is that thing by construction:

1. EVALUATION AND DEVELOPMENT — FREE. You may use this package to
   evaluate the Engine, develop against it, run tests and internal
   prototypes, without charge and without asking anyone.

2. DISTRIBUTION REQUIRES A COMMERCIAL LICENSE. Shipping an application,
   device, or offering that includes this package — an app store
   release, an enterprise deployment to third parties, a product that
   carries the Engine inside it — is distribution of the Engine, and
   requires a commercial license from the Licensor. This is the same
   rule the Engine itself carries; this package merely states it up
   front, because embedding is what this package is for.

3. WHAT STAYS FREE. Applications whose users reach YOUR servers, where
   the Engine runs server-side for your own business, are governed by
   the Engine's own source-available terms (free for your own
   production use). This package's rule concerns the Engine leaving
   your hands inside a distributed artifact.

4. COMMERCIAL LICENSING. Terms are negotiated directly and are
   intentionally simple. Contact: barisakin@gmail.com
   (see COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md in the OxiDB repository).

5. NO WARRANTY. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF
   ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE
   WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND
   NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE LICENSOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY
